    Gridsmith is a retro pixel-art to SVG editor and a dependency-free
    JavaScript library (engine.js) for quantizing images onto a pixel grid and
    exporting SVG. It is produced by Martial Systems LLC / Martial Games.

    WHAT WAS USED HERE
    ------------------
    The two-pass rectangle merging strategy in the mergedRects() function of
    index.html is adapted from Gridsmith's gridToSvg() (engine.js):

      Pass 1 collapses each row of filled cells into horizontal runs of a
      single colour.
      Pass 2 stacks vertically-adjacent runs that share the same x origin and
      width into taller rectangles.

    The purpose is to keep exported SVGs small: a solid 32x32 block is 1024
    cells but becomes a single <rect> rather than 1024 of them.

    This project is an independent implementation and is not affiliated with,
    endorsed by, or sponsored by Martial Systems LLC or Martial Games. It is
    not the official Gridsmith, and the official hosted product and API are
    separate works by their authors.

    The adaptation is also noted in a source comment at the top of
    mergedRects() in index.html.

